{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "SOMA Software - Aviation Management API",
    "description": "# SOMA Software Public API\n\nSOMA Software's comprehensive API for aviation operations management, designed to integrate seamlessly with external systems for inventory control, fleet management, maintenance tracking, and procurement logistics.\n\n---\n\n## Release Notes - v1.0.0\n\n**Release Date:** December 2025\n\n### Highlights\n\n| Category | Endpoints | Features |\n|----------|-----------|----------|\n| Authentication | 1 | JWT token-based access |\n| Reference Lists | 17 | Geographic, component, aircraft, personnel data |\n| Personnel | 2 | Query and create personnel |\n| Catalog | 6 | Component management (10 types supported) |\n| Inventory | 6 | Warehouse, aircraft, workshop, dispatch tracking |\n| Fleet | 2 | Aircraft registration and queries |\n| Warehouses | 2 | Storage location management |\n| Suppliers | 2 | Vendor management |\n| Requisitions | 2 | Multi-item requisition support |\n| Procurement | 4 | Purchase orders, currencies, terms |\n| Maintenance | 2 | Discrepancies and work orders |\n\n**Total: 48 endpoints**\n\n---\n### API Credentials\n\nAPI credentials are issued exclusively by SOMA Software Technical Support. Contact [https://www.somasoftware.com/support](https://www.somasoftware.com/support) to request access.\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nThis API enables aviation operators, MROs (Maintenance, Repair, and Overhaul organizations), and enterprise systems to:\n\n- **Catalog Management**: Create, query, and manage aeronautical components with full traceability\n- **Inventory Control**: Track components across warehouses, workshops, and installed on aircraft\n- **Fleet Management**: Aircraft registration, configuration, and technical data management\n- **Personnel Management**: Register and manage organizational personnel\n- **Procurement & Logistics**: Requisitions, purchase orders, and supplier management\n\n---\n\n## Authentication\n\nThe API uses a **two-layer authentication system**:\n\n### Step 1: Basic Authentication (API Access)\n\nThe login endpoint requires **HTTP Basic Authentication** with the following public API credentials:\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|-----------|-------|\n| **Username** | `public_soma_api` |\n| **Password** | `hidden` |\n\nFor security purposes, the public API key is not published in this documentation. To obtain your API credentials, please submit a request to SOMA Software Technical Support at [https://www.somasoftware.com/support](https://www.somasoftware.com/support)\n\n### Step 2: JWT Bearer Token (Request Authorization)\n\nAfter successful login, use the returned JWT token for all subsequent requests:\n\n```http\nAuthorization: Bearer <your_jwt_token>\n```\n\n### Token Lifecycle\n\n- Tokens have a limited validity period\n- Implement automatic token refresh in your integration\n- Store tokens securely and never expose them in client-side code\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### 1. Authenticate\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"https://api.somasoftware.com/soma-api-public/api/auth/login\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Basic cHVibGljX3NvbWFfYXBpOlh5NyRQcTkhTG0yQFJ0NSNaazheVnczJk5oNipKZDE=\" \\\n  -d '{\"username\": \"YOUR_ACCOUNT@YOUR_COMPANY.com\", \"password\": \"YOUR_PASSWORD\"}'\n```\n\n### 2. Use the Token\n```bash\ncurl -X GET \"https://api.somasoftware.com/soma-api-public/api/airship\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token_from_step_1>\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## HTTP Status Codes\n\n| Code | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `200` | Successful operation |\n| `400` | Bad request - Invalid or incomplete data |\n| `401` | Unauthorized - Invalid or expired token |\n| `404` | Resource not found |\n| `409` | Conflict - Resource already exists |\n| `500` | Internal server error |\n\n---\n\n## Rate Limiting\n\nStandard rate limits apply to all endpoints. Contact SOMA Software Support for enterprise rate limit increases.\n\n---\n\n## Support & Resources\n\n- **Technical Support**: [https://www.somasoftware.com/support](https://www.somasoftware.com/support)\n- **Email**: technicalsupport@somasoftware.com\n",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "contact": {
      "name": "SOMA Software Technical Support",
      "email": "technicalsupport@somasoftware.com",
      "url": "https://www.somasoftware.com/support"
    },
    "license": {
      "name": "Proprietary License",
      "url": "https://www.somasoftware.com/privacy-policy"
    },
    "x-logo": {
      "url": "https://www.somasoftware.com/logo.png",
      "altText": "SOMA Software Logo"
    },
    "x-jentic-source-url": "https://api.swaggerhub.com/apis/somasoftware/soma-public-api/1.0.0"
  },
  "externalDocs": {
    "description": "SOMA Software Support Portal",
    "url": "https://www.somasoftware.com/support"
  },
